Good morning, Jules,

Executive Summary

This executive adverse news briefing covers 9 material incidents for UK banki=
ng and financial entities during 12=E2=80=9319 October 2026. The period was m=
arked by heightened regulatory scrutiny, with the FCA placing Jarvis Investme=
nt Management and ePayments Systems into special administration and Aldermore=
 Bank facing =C2=A3750 million in motor finance redress provisions ahead of U=
pper Tribunal hearings in February 2027. Financial crime risks included FCA a=
rrests for insider dealing and a =C2=A32 million investment fraud prosecution=
, while operational resilience concerns emerged from a cyber attack on ABC In=
ternational Bank, phishing warnings from NatWest, and payment processing fail=
ures at Nationwide and Co-operative Bank.

1. Regulatory Enforcement & Legal Risks

Jarvis Investment Management & ePayments Systems: On 14 and 15 October 2026, =
the FCA announced that both Jarvis Investment Management Limited and ePayment=
s Systems Limited entered special administration under court-appointed insolv=
ency practitioners due to capital adequacy and operational compliance failure=
s, freezing client assets and operations.
Source: https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/jarvis-investment-management=
-limited-enters-special-administration

UK Financial Sector Governance (FCA Multi-Firm Review): On 12 October 2026, t=
he FCA published multi-firm governance review findings establishing mandatory=
 expectations for UK banks, benchmark administrators, and financial instituti=
ons to strengthen board challenge, record decision-making, and ensure clear o=
versight of executive actions.
Source: https://www.globalfinregblog.com/2026/10/fca-sets-out-expectations-on=
-firms-governance-arrangements/

UK Asset Management & Banking Wealth Units (FCA CP26/35): On 16 October 2026,=
 the FCA published Consultation Paper CP26/35 proposing mandatory 90-day mini=
mum notice periods and monthly redemption limits for funds investing in illiq=
uid assets, requiring UK wealth management and banking divisions to re-archit=
ect product liquidity terms.
Source: https://www.simmons-simmons.com/en/publications/cmvakk46l00xoudt0lst0=
uji8/cp26-35-redemption-terms-for-funds-investing-in-illiquid-assets

Aldermore Bank Plc: On 13 October 2026, the UK Upper Tribunal scheduled heari=
ngs for February 16=E2=80=9326, 2027, to hear lender challenges against the F=
CA's motor finance redress scheme. Parent company FirstRand put the bank up f=
or sale due to redress exposure and financial strain after setting aside =C2=
=A3750 million in motor finance mis-selling provisions.
Source: https://www.cityam.com/motor-finance-legal-battle-set-for-february-20=
27/

2. Financial Crime & Compliance Risks

UK Banking Sector (NatWest, Lloyds, Santander): Industry analysis published o=
n 16 October 2026 highlighted customer friction over new Authorised Push Paym=
ent (APP) fraud reimbursement rules, with major lenders confirming they will =
deduct a fixed =C2=A3100 excess on customer scam claims.
Source: https://www.clearscore.com/learn/managing-money/bank-fraud-scam-exces=
s-charge

Financial Conduct Authority (FCA Operations): On 13 October 2026, the FCA ann=
ounced three arrests in a major enforcement operation targeting an active cri=
minal insider dealing ring.
Source: https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/three-arrests-major-fca-op=
eration-against-criminal-insider-dealing-ring

Financial Conduct Authority (FCA Prosecution): On 12 October 2026, two indivi=
duals pleaded guilty at Portsmouth Crown Court in an FCA criminal prosecution=
 after clients lost =C2=A32 million in an unauthorized investment fraud schem=
e.
Source: https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/two-plead-guilty-after-cli=
ents-lose-2m-fraud-case

3. Operational & Cybersecurity Risks

ABC International Bank Plc: On 18 October 2026, a cyber attack via an IT serv=
ice provider's online-banking systems left customer login unavailable for thr=
ee days. The bank stated that unauthorised parties accessed individual system=
 components at the provider, but no accounts or payments were affected, and t=
here was no spread to other systems.
Source: https://borncity.com/blog/2026/10/18/cyberangriff-auf-abc-bank-connec=
twise-cloud-backup-kompromittierung/

National Westminster Bank Public Limited Company: On 17 October 2026, NatWest=
 warned customers about fraudulent phishing emails mimicking the bank's brand=
ing and asking recipients to review and update their personal details. No con=
firmed losses or breach of bank systems were reported.
Source: https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/news/cost-of-living/natwest-issues-w=
arning-over-email-34752474

Kind regards, Tiago Vieira

